# Graphify first (1200-token budget)

This repo has a knowledge graph at `graphify-out/`. Keep it current with `graphify watch .` (AST rebuilds on code changes; no extra process manager).

**Before Read, Grep, Glob, or Shell exploration, query the graph first.** This applies to you and every subagent you spawn — pass this rule into those prompts.

```bash
graphify query "<question>" --budget 1200
```

- Relationships: `graphify path "<A>" "<B>"`
- One concept: `graphify explain "<concept>"`
- Hubs only if needed: `graphify god-nodes --top 8`

Do **not** read all of `GRAPH_REPORT.md` (it is large). Stay inside the 1200-token query result, then open only cited source files.

Skip graphify only when `graphify-out/graph.json` is missing, or the user says not to use it. Dirty `graphify-out/` files are expected.

Do **not** run `graphify update .` after every edit — `graphify watch` and the post-commit hook do AST rebuilds. Run `graphify update .` only if watch is not running or `graphify-out/needs_update` exists.

The graph is a map, not a substitute for reading the exact lines you will edit.

## Complementary: RTK

RTK compresses **Shell** output (git, pnpm, lint, test, next build). Cursor rewrites those commands automatically. Do not re-run a command just to get full logs; if output is insufficient, read the tee path printed on failure.
